WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.024
This slide compares three terms that are

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.379
sometimes used loosely module package and library

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:07.960
A module is the smallest of the

00:00:07.987 --> 00:00:11.118
three concepts in this comparison It is

00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:13.947
usually one Python file that contains reusable

00:00:13.974 --> 00:00:17.605
code Examples include the built-in math module

00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:19.421
or a file that we create ourselves

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:22.658
such as calculations dot P Y A

00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:24.763
package is a folder that groups related

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:28.618
modules For example a package named analytics

00:00:28.645 --> 00:00:30.895
could contain finance dot P Y health

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:32.763
dot P Y and reporting dot P

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:35.947
Y A library is a larger collection

00:00:35.974 --> 00:00:39.895
of reusable tools Libraries may contain several

00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:43.868
packages and many modules NumPy and Pandas

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:46.289
are good examples of widely used libraries

00:00:46.316 --> 00:00:49.276
in data analytics A simple way to

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:52.934
remember the relationship is this Module means

00:00:52.961 --> 00:00:57.553
file Package means folder Library means a

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.368
larger reusable collection of tools The exact

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:04.039
technical details can become more complicated in

00:01:04.053 --> 00:01:07.118
professional software development but this simple
model

00:01:07.145 --> 00:01:09.684
is enough for our course Use a

00:01:09.697 --> 00:01:11.408
module when one file can hold a

00:01:11.421 --> 00:01:14.803
related set of functions or constants Use

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:16.987
a package when the project contains several

00:01:17.013 --> 00:01:19.355
related modules that should be grouped together

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:22.382
Use a library when a larger collection

00:01:22.408 --> 00:01:24.592
of reusable tools is shared across many

00:01:24.618 --> 00:01:27.566
tasks or projects As we move into

00:01:27.592 --> 00:01:29.816
NumPy and Pandas later in the course

00:01:30.105 --> 00:01:31.763
you will see that importing a library

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:33.961
gives us access to many organized tools

00:01:33.987 --> 00:01:36.250
that other developers have already created and

00:01:36.276 --> 00:01:36.763
tested
